text: <|channel|>analysis<|message|>We need to answer: "When does it get slow?" The user previously asked: "Explain what a hash table is and why lookups are fast." The assistant responded with a description. Now the user asks: "When does it get slow?" So we need to explain scenarios where hash table performance degrades: collisions, load factor high, poor hash function, rehashing, memory overhead, cache misses, etc. Also mention that worst-case lookup is O(n) if all keys collide. Also mention that deletion/insertion may be slower if rehashing. Also mention that if the hash table is too small relative to number of elements, collisions increase. Also mention that if the hash function is poor, many collisions. Also mention that if the keys are not well distributed, or if the table is not resized properly. Also mention that if the table is too large, memory overhead and cache misses degrade performance. Also mention that if the table is used in a multi-threaded
